---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import FAQSection from '../../components/FAQSection.astro';

const title = "Battery Industry Weekly — Week 29, 2026 | Battery Calculators";
const description = "This week in batteries: Leaked EU plan recognises a need for 200GW of storage by 2030, Giga Storage finances a 700MW/2.8GWh battery in Belgium, and Lazard says US utility-scale storage costs have risen.";
const canonical = "https://batterycalculators.com/news/battery-industry-weekly-2026-week-29";
const publishDate = "2026-08-08";
const lastUpdated = "2026-08-08";
const readingTime = 16;

const faqItems = [
  {
    "question": "What is the Battery Industry Weekly?",
    "answer": "A short editorial digest covering the most important battery industry news each week — EV batteries, grid-scale storage, regulation, manufacturing, and research."
  },
  {
    "question": "How are stories selected?",
    "answer": "The generator fetches RSS feeds from trusted sources, deduplicates similar stories, scores them by relevance, and selects the top stories for the week."
  },
  {
    "question": "When is the digest published?",
    "answer": "A new edition is generated every Friday covering the current week."
  }
];

const breadcrumbs = [
  { label: 'News', href: '/news/' },
  { label: 'Week 29, 2026' },
];
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  ogType="article"
  schema="webApplication"
  schemaName="Battery Industry Weekly — Week 29, 2026"
  schemaDescription={description}
  faqItems={faqItems}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-12 border-b border-hairline pb-8">
      <a href="/news/" class="text-label-uppercase text-xs text-muted hover:text-primary transition-colors mb-4 inline-block">&larr; Back to News</a>
      <Breadcrumb items={breadcrumbs} />
      <span class="text-label-uppercase text-m-blue-light text-xs block mb-4">WEEKLY EDITION</span>
      <h1 class="text-display-md text-primary mb-4">Battery Industry Weekly — Week 29</h1>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4 text-caption text-muted mb-6">
        <span>Jul 13 – Jul 19, 2026</span>
        <span>{readingTime} min read</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-body-md text-body font-light">
        This week in batteries: Leaked EU plan recognises a need for 200GW of storage by 2030, Giga Storage finances a 700MW/2.8GWh battery in Belgium, and Lazard says US utility-scale storage costs have risen.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Story 1 -->
    <section class="mb-12">
      <span class="text-label-uppercase text-m-blue-light text-[10px] block mb-2">REGULATION</span>
      <h2 class="text-title-xl text-primary mb-4">Leaked EU plan recognises a need for 200GW of storage by 2030</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md text-body font-light mb-4">Energy-Storage.News reported on 13 July 2026 that a leaked draft of the EU Electrification Action Plan says the bloc needs 200GW of energy storage by 2030. A 16 July update in the same article says Energy Storage Europe welcomed the ambition and warned that faster electrification will require substantially more flexibility and coordinated regulation.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Story 2 -->
    <section class="mb-12 border-t border-hairline pt-12">
      <span class="text-label-uppercase text-m-blue-light text-[10px] block mb-2">BESS</span>
      <h2 class="text-title-xl text-primary mb-4">Giga Storage finances a 700MW/2.8GWh battery in Belgium</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md text-body font-light mb-4">Giga Storage has secured a €450 million (US$512 million) package for its 700MW/2,800MWh Green Turtle project in Belgium. Energy-Storage.News reported on 14 July 2026 that the debt, from a consortium of 10 banks, was announced on 10 July, with the remaining equity from InfraVia Capital Partners.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Story 3 -->
    <section class="mb-12 border-t border-hairline pt-12">
      <span class="text-label-uppercase text-m-blue-light text-[10px] block mb-2">BESS</span>
      <h2 class="text-title-xl text-primary mb-4">Lazard says US utility-scale storage costs have risen</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md text-body font-light mb-4">Lazard’s 11th levelised-cost-of-storage analysis says US utility-scale battery costs have risen, reversing the declines in its 2025 edition, because tariffs and foreign-entity-of-concern limits on the investment tax credit have cut off cheaper Chinese cells. For a 100MW/400MWh system, Energy-Storage.News reported on 14 July 2026 that Lazard’s 2025 range was US$115–254/MWh without the tax credit and US$83–192/MWh with it, against US$210–292/MWh and US$148–209/MWh this year.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Story 4 -->
    <section class="mb-12 border-t border-hairline pt-12">
      <span class="text-label-uppercase text-m-blue-light text-[10px] block mb-2">BESS</span>
      <h2 class="text-title-xl text-primary mb-4">CSIRO’s GenCost update raises pumped-hydro costs and lowers battery costs</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md text-body font-light mb-4">Australia’s CSIRO has raised pumped-hydro cost estimates and lowered battery-storage cost estimates in the final GenCost 2025-26 report, Energy-Storage.News reported on 15 July 2026.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Story 5 -->
    <section class="mb-12 border-t border-hairline pt-12">
      <span class="text-label-uppercase text-m-blue-light text-[10px] block mb-2">BESS</span>
      <h2 class="text-title-xl text-primary mb-4">Global large-scale storage additions rose 27% in the first half of 2026</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md text-body font-light mb-4">Energy-Storage.News reported on 15 July 2026 that large-scale battery deployments were up 27% in the first half of 2026, and that 9.1GW/33.5GWh came online in June, with Saudi Arabia accounting for more than one-third of that monthly total.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Story 6 -->
    <section class="mb-12 border-t border-hairline pt-12">
      <span class="text-label-uppercase text-m-blue-light text-[10px] block mb-2">BESS</span>
      <h2 class="text-title-xl text-primary mb-4">Australia adds more than 4GWh of storage to its renewable priority list</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md text-body font-light mb-4">Australia’s federal government has added 11 generation and storage projects to its National Renewable Energy Priority List, including more than 4GWh of battery storage, Energy-Storage.News reported on 15 July 2026.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Story 7 -->
    <section class="mb-12 border-t border-hairline pt-12">
      <span class="text-label-uppercase text-m-blue-light text-[10px] block mb-2">BESS</span>
      <h2 class="text-title-xl text-primary mb-4">Transgrid opens a path for 900MW of grid-forming batteries in New South Wales</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md text-body font-light mb-4">Transgrid has opened a pathway for 900MW of grid-forming battery storage to count toward New South Wales’ minimum system-strength requirement, after synchronous-condenser costs rose 38%, Energy-Storage.News reported on 16 July 2026.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Story 8 -->
    <section class="mb-12 border-t border-hairline pt-12">
      <span class="text-label-uppercase text-m-blue-light text-[10px] block mb-2">BESS</span>
      <h2 class="text-title-xl text-primary mb-4">Avantus and Fluence advance two solar-plus-storage projects in California</h2>
      <p class="text-body-md text-body font-light mb-4">Avantus and Fluence are moving ahead with two solar-plus-storage projects in California, with Fluence supplying domestic-content battery systems, Energy-Storage.News reported on 15 July 2026.</p>
    </section>

    <!-- Sources -->
    <section class="mb-12 border-t border-hairline pt-12">
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-primary mb-4">Sources</h2>
      <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2 text-body-sm text-muted list-disc pl-5">
        <li><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/leaked-eu-electrification-action-plan-recognises-need-for-200gw-of-energy-storage-by-2030/" class="text-m-blue-light hover:text-primary transition-colors" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Leaked EU Electrification Action Plan recognises need for 200GW of energy storage by 2030 — Energy-Storage.News</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/giga-storage-secures-finance-for-2-8gwh-critical-infrastructure-belgium-bess/" class="text-m-blue-light hover:text-primary transition-colors" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Giga Storage secures finance for 2.8GWh critical infrastructure Belgium BESS — Energy-Storage.News</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/lazard-us-utility-scale-energy-storage-lcos-has-increased-since-restrictions-on-chinese-cells-came-into-force/" class="text-m-blue-light hover:text-primary transition-colors" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Lazard: US utility-scale energy storage LCOS has increased since restrictions on Chinese cells came into force — Energy-Storage.News</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/pumped-hydro-costs-revised-up-battery-storage-costs-down-as-australias-csiro-publishes-final-gencost-2025-26-report/" class="text-m-blue-light hover:text-primary transition-colors" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pumped hydro costs revised up, battery storage costs down, as Australia’s CSIRO publishes final GenCost 2025-26 report — Energy-Storage.News</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/global-bess-deployments-soar-27-in-h1-2026-saudi-arabia-drives-figures-in-june/" class="text-m-blue-light hover:text-primary transition-colors" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Global BESS deployments soar 27% in H1 2026, Saudi Arabia drives figures in June — Energy-Storage.News</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/over-4gwh-of-battery-storage-added-to-australias-updated-national-renewable-energy-priority-list/" class="text-m-blue-light hover:text-primary transition-colors" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Over 4GWh of battery storage added to Australia’s updated National Renewable Energy Priority List — Energy-Storage.News</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/australias-transgrid-opens-pathway-for-900mw-of-grid-forming-battery-storage-as-synchronous-condenser-costs-surge-38/" class="text-m-blue-light hover:text-primary transition-colors" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Australia’s Transgrid opens pathway for 900MW of grid-forming battery storage as synchronous condenser costs surge 38% — Energy-Storage.News</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://www.energy-storage.news/avantus-progresses-california-solar-plus-storage-projects-fluence-providing-domestic-content-bess/" class="text-m-blue-light hover:text-primary transition-colors" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Avantus progresses California solar-plus-storage projects, Fluence providing domestic content BESS — Energy-Storage.News</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <FAQSection items={faqItems} />

    <!-- Disclaimer -->
    <section class="mb-16 border-t border-hairline pt-12">
      <div class="bg-surface-elevated border border-hairline p-6">
        <h3 class="text-title-lg text-primary mb-3">Disclaimer</h3>
        <p class="text-body-sm text-muted">
          This article summarizes publicly available news and analysis. BatteryCalculators.com does not guarantee the accuracy of third-party information. Always verify facts with primary sources before making engineering or procurement decisions. This content is provided for informational purposes only and does not constitute professional engineering advice.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </article>
</Layout>
